+The smooth polar meets (E_1) at (Z=1). The cusp has
+((v,U,Z)\sim(t^2,-t^2/c_1,\lambda t)), so after resolving the A1 it passes
+through the node (E_1\cap E_2), contributing once to each component. Thus
